      "problem": "If $x=-4$ and $y=3,$ then $\\frac{3x+2}{3}+\\frac{x+y}{2y}=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Replacing $x$ with $-4$ and $y$ with $3$ in the expression, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x+2}{3}+\\frac{x+y}{2y} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(-4)+2}{3}+\\frac{-4+3}{2(3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-12+2}{3}+\\frac{(-1)}{6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{10}{3}-\\frac{1}{6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{20}{6}-\\frac{1}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{-20-1}{6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{21}{6} & = \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
